openai/math (mathematical substrate index)
------------------------------------------

`src/rain/mathematics/data/openai-math.json` is derived from the catalogue of
`openai/math` (https://github.com/openai/math) at commit
adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a: result-family titles and summaries
(CONTENTS.md), disciplines (overview.tex), manuscript titles and abstracts,
citations and attribution notes as each manuscript's README gives them, the
Lean formalization catalogue's fields (lean/formalization.yaml), the Lean scope
pages' text and the comparator configs' declaration names. It was reformatted
into JSON with per-file SHA-256 by `scripts/math-substrate.ts`; nothing else was
changed. No manuscript PDF, LaTeX source, Lean source or reasoning-summary PDF
is copied: they are named by path at that commit and never fetched. The
repository is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, reproduced in
full in `src/rain/mathematics/data/LICENSE.md`; it carries no NOTICE file. As
the repository says, its manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model,
some with human assistance (each such note is kept with its manuscript), and
its Lean formalizations build on third-party libraries it lists (mathlib4 and
others), each under its own licence; none of them is included here.

FlyBody (the digital fly's body model)
--------------------------------------

`src/bethesda/fly/data/flybody-skeleton.json`, `flybody-lod0.json` and
`flybody-lod1.json` are derived from TuragaLab/flybody
(https://github.com/TuragaLab/flybody, commit
d015e9bfe441bd90ae431bac24c55cb74bdbce26): `flybody/fruitfly/assets/fruitfly.xml`
and the OBJ meshes it names. FlyBody is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, reproduced in full in `src/bethesda/fly/data/LICENSE.md`; it
carries no NOTICE file. The files were modified: visual meshes only, transformed
into their body frames, merged, welded and decimated to two levels of detail,
quantised, with texture coordinates and normals dropped and the skeleton
transcribed from the MJCF. `flybody.source.json` lists every modification with
per-file hashes. FlyBody's figshare datasets (trained policies and reference
trajectories, GPL-3.0) are not included. Cite: Vaxenburg R, Siwanowicz I,
Merel J, et al. Whole-body physics simulation of fruit fly locomotion. Nature
643, 1312-1320 (2025). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-09029-4

Virtual Fly Brain (the digital fly's neuroanatomical reference)
---------------------------------------------------------------

`src/bethesda/fly/data/vfb-reference.json` holds identifiers, labels,
definitions, licence metadata and class-level connectivity counts retrieved
from the Virtual Fly Brain API (https://v3-cached.virtualflybrain.org) by
`scripts/import-vfb-reference.ts`, with each response's hash and the retrieval
time. FBbt class labels and definitions are from the FlyBase Drosophila anatomy
ontology, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
VFB reports the JRC2018Unisex template (VFB_00101567) and its painted neuropil
domains under CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0; none of their geometry is included, and the
fly's panel links to VFB instead. Cite: Court R, Costa M, Pilgrim C, et al.
Virtual Fly Brain - an interactive atlas of the Drosophila nervous system.
Front. Physiol. 14:1076533 (2023). https://doi.org/10.3389/fphys.2023.1076533

Grooming ethograms (the digital fly's grooming calibration)
-----------------------------------------------------------

`src/bethesda/fly/data/grooming-reference.json` holds summary statistics that
`scripts/import-fly-grooming.ts` computed from the per-frame ethograms of dusted
and undusted Canton S flies (`CantonS_dusted.mat`, `CantonS_undusted.mat`) and
constants read from the model code (`groomingmodel.m`) of the dataset Zhang N,
Guo L, Simpson JH. Spatial comparisons of mechanosensory information govern the
grooming sequence in Drosophila. Mendeley Data, V1 (2020),
https://doi.org/10.17632/fxz8dgywcd.1, licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The ethograms were reduced to
summary statistics; no per-frame data are kept, and the file records each
source file's hash and the retrieval time. The paper it accompanies: Zhang N,
Guo L, Simpson JH. Curr Biol 30:988-1001 (2020),
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2020.01.045.

ECHO olfactory research extension (src/bethesda/life/foraging/)
------------------------------------------------------------
The behavioral odor ON/OFF filters independently implement equations 8–13
and Table 1 ACF time constants from:
Álvarez-Salvado E, Licata AM, Connor EG, McHugh MK, King BMN, Stavropoulos N,
Victor JD, Crimaldi JP, Nagel KI. Elementary sensory-motor transformations
underlying olfactory navigation in walking fruit-flies. eLife 7:e37815 (2018).
https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.37815
No authors' source code, figures, trajectories or datasets are included.
Motor integration and ECHO odor normalization are separately identified model
choices. This is a behavioral filter implementation, not a neuron reconstruction.

Connectome research backend (fly-neural/)
-----------------------------------------
No FlyWire data are included in this repository. `python -m fly_neural
acquire` downloads FlyWire's public release v783 (Zenodo 10676866), the
flyconnectome/flywire_annotations v3.2.0 table and four files of
philshiu/Drosophila_brain_model (commit 91bdd1e) into a local cache, only on
the user's explicit acceptance of their terms, and verifies each by SHA-256
(`fly-neural/fly_neural/sources.py`). FlyWire data are CC BY-NC 4.0
(https://flywire.ai/guidelines): cite Dorkenwald S, et al. Nature 634,
124-138 (2024), https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07558-y, and Schlegel P,
et al. Nature 634, 139-152 (2024), https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07686-5.
The model is that of Shiu P, et al. A Drosophila computational brain model
reveals sensorimotor processing. Nature 634, 210-219 (2024),
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07763-9; their code is MIT-licensed and is
not copied: `fly-neural/fly_neural/lif.py` is an independent implementation
of the equations and parameters the paper states, and their `model.py` is run
unmodified from the cache as a reference. `fly-neural/fly_neural/populations.py`
lists neuron root ids that Shiu et al.'s `figures.ipynb` names (MIT).
`fly-neural/tests/data/brian2_conformance.json` is Brian 2's output for that
`model.py` on synthetic networks and contains no FlyWire data. The results in
`docs/benchmarks/fly-neural/` are model outputs derived from FlyWire data and
carry its terms (`docs/benchmarks/fly-neural/LICENSE.md`).

No BANC data are included either. BANC v888 (the brain and ventral nerve
cord connectome) is read only from two tables a person downloads from FlyWire
Codex and pins by SHA-256 outside the repository; `fly-neural/fly_neural/banc.py`
records the reviewed hashes and accepts no other bytes. BANC data are CC BY 4.0
(BANC project; Harvard Dataverse, https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/7WTH1N): cite
Bates AS, et al. Distributed control circuits across a brain-and-cord
connectome. Nature (2026), https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-026-10735-w, and the
Dataverse deposit. The results in `docs/benchmarks/fly-neural/banc/` are model
outputs derived from BANC data and carry its terms
(`docs/benchmarks/fly-neural/banc/LICENSE.md`).
